		{
			dependencies: [
				"1FF464B087641964"
				"48BA4FE3846FD45B"
			]
			dependency_requirement: "one_completed"
			description: [
				"Using Hell Shelves or Sea Shelves you may have noticed that you have gained access to higher level enchantments. There are three stats associated with enchanting that you may have also noticed; not all of which always work in your favor."
				""
				"Eterna is the enchanting level provided by your book shelves. A level 30 enchanting set up will have 15 eterna and a level 45 will have 22.5 eterna. Upon adding your 5 Hell or Sea Shelves you will reach 22.5 eterna."
				""
				"Quanta increases variance in enchanting levels meaning you may see higher or lower levels of enchants more regularly making it harder to obtain high level enchants more regularly. Higher quanta means more variance; which can be benificial if you have high Rectification. Rectification helps to negate the appearance of lower levels enchants."
				""
				"Arcana makes rarer enchants more common and common enchants less common at higher values allowing you to switch between what enchament rarity is most likely by altering your set up. Slightly increasing Arcana values is good for increasing the number of enchantments you recieve."
			]
			id: "602493BF0C75341F"
			rewards: [
